---
source: crates/psptool-cli/tests/help.rs
expression: "render_help(&[\"replace\", \"--help\"])"
---
Replace an entry body (and optionally re-sign)

Usage: psptool replace [OPTIONS] --directory-index <DIRECTORY_INDEX> --file-index <FILE_INDEX> --outfile <OUTFILE> <FILE>

Arguments:
  <FILE>  

Options:
  -r, --rom-index <ROM_INDEX>
          [default: 0]
  -d, --directory-index <DIRECTORY_INDEX>
          Required
  -e, --file-index <FILE_INDEX>
          Required
  -o, --outfile <OUTFILE>
          Required
  -s, --subfile <SUBFILE>
          Replacement file contents. When omitted, this becomes a "plain re-sign" of the entry (requires `-p`)
  -p, --privkey <PRIVKEY>
          Private key (PEM) for re-signing [aliases: --privkeystub]
  -a, --privkeypass <PRIVKEY_PASS>
          Passphrase (currently ignored — `rsa::pkcs8::DecodePrivateKey` reads PEM directly; encrypted-PEM support is a follow-up)
  -h, --help
          Print help
